WEBVTT

00:00:00.550 --> 00:00:02.445
Lesson 13.1.

00:00:02.445 --> 00:00:05.100
Income sources ranked by durability.

00:00:05.100 --> 00:00:07.101
By the end of this lesson, you'll

00:00:07.101 --> 00:00:09.102
be able to rank income sources by

00:00:09.102 --> 00:00:11.515
how long and how reliably they're likely

00:00:11.515 --> 00:00:13.575
to pay, not by their headline rate.

00:00:14.875 --> 00:00:16.165
Here's the plan.

00:00:16.165 --> 00:00:17.850
First, the key ideas.

00:00:17.850 --> 00:00:19.375
Then, your checklist.

00:00:19.375 --> 00:00:21.537
And finally, a three-question quiz.

00:00:22.837 --> 00:00:25.279
A durable income engine is built mostly

00:00:25.279 --> 00:00:27.227
from the top of this table.

00:00:27.227 --> 00:00:29.427
The bottom rows are boosters you size

00:00:29.427 --> 00:00:31.522
small and expect to switch off.

00:00:31.522 --> 00:00:34.592
Blue-chip stablecoin lending, Borrower demand,

00:00:34.592 --> 00:00:36.982
High, Medium: moves with demand.

00:00:36.982 --> 00:00:42.762
Staking / LSTs, Network security rewards, High, Low–medium.

00:00:42.762 --> 00:00:45.945
Fixed-rate PTs to maturity, Locked at purchase,

00:00:45.945 --> 00:00:48.897
Fixed for the term, None until maturity.

00:00:48.897 --> 00:00:51.729
Curated lending vaults, Borrower demand

00:00:51.729 --> 00:00:54.577
in isolated markets, Medium, Medium.

00:00:54.577 --> 00:00:58.447
LP fees (major pairs), Trading volume, Medium, High.

00:00:58.447 --> 00:01:01.291
Funding / basis carry, Market positioning,

00:01:01.291 --> 00:01:03.672
Low–medium, High: can turn negative.

00:01:04.972 --> 00:01:08.142
Options premium, Volatility, Medium, High.

00:01:08.142 --> 00:01:11.752
Incentives / points, Protocol budgets, Low, Very high.

00:01:13.052 --> 00:01:14.512
Here's your checklist.

00:01:14.512 --> 00:01:16.047
Do it now, for real.

00:01:16.047 --> 00:01:18.161
First, every income position tagged

00:01:18.161 --> 00:01:20.282
with its source and durability.

00:01:20.282 --> 00:01:23.562
And finally, Core income from high-durability sources.

00:01:24.863 --> 00:01:26.073
Question 1.

00:01:26.073 --> 00:01:28.228
Why is funding carry low durability?

00:01:32.648 --> 00:01:35.291
The answer: It depends on market positioning

00:01:35.291 --> 00:01:37.582
and can turn negative for long periods.

00:01:38.882 --> 00:01:40.127
Question 2.

00:01:40.127 --> 00:01:41.457
Which source gives a known

00:01:41.457 --> 00:01:42.442
rate for a set term?

00:01:46.862 --> 00:01:49.807
The answer: Fixed-rate PTs held to maturity.

00:01:51.107 --> 00:01:52.377
Question 3.

00:01:52.377 --> 00:01:54.402
How should incentive income be treated?

00:01:58.822 --> 00:02:01.355
The answer: As a temporary booster, sold

00:02:01.355 --> 00:02:03.332
on a schedule and not relied on.

00:02:04.632 --> 00:02:07.147
Do the checklist now, before you move on.

00:02:07.147 --> 00:02:12.721
Next up, Lesson 13.2: Risk-adjusted yield: subtracting expected losses.
